diff --git a/saas/AGENTS.md b/saas/AGENTS.md
index 5408713..9ef4f4a 100644
--- a/saas/AGENTS.md
+++ b/saas/AGENTS.md
@@ -8,6 +8,12 @@
 
 `saas:enable` is a prerequisite for deploying, not just for local development. Only under that flag does `bin/kamal` pass `-c` pointing at this gem's `config/deploy.yml`. Skip it and Kamal reads the root `config/deploy.yml` instead — the self-hosting example, which knows nothing about our destinations.
 
+## Billing
+
+`Plan` is the catalogue: Free (1,000 cards, 1 GB), Unlimited ($20/month, 5 GB), Unlimited+ ($25/month, 500 GB). `Account::Billing` carries what an account is entitled to — `plan`, `card_limit`, `storage_limit`, `comped?` — and the limits the controllers and the views check. Stripe owns checkout, the customer portal, and the truth about subscription changes, which arrive at `/stripe/webhooks`.
+
+`account_overridden_limits` is support's override of what an account counts for (card count, bytes used), and `account_billing_waivers` marks an account as comped. Both are managed from `admin/accounts`. An account cancelled in the app has its Stripe subscription cancelled too, so nobody is billed for a closed account.
+
 ## Deploy
 
 Pre-deploy: `bin/rails saas:enable`
diff --git a/saas/README.md b/saas/README.md
index 28b0891..70fa031 100644
--- a/saas/README.md
+++ b/saas/README.md
@@ -40,6 +40,30 @@ bin/dev # You need to start the dev server in the same terminal session
 
 This will ask for your 1password authorization to read and set the environment variables that Stripe needs.
 
+### Plans
+
+| Plan        | Price     | Cards     | Storage |
+|-------------|-----------|-----------|---------|
+| Free        | $0        | 1,000     | 1 GB    |
+| Unlimited   | $20/month | unlimited | 5 GB    |
+| Unlimited+  | $25/month | unlimited | 500 GB  |
+
+The plans are defined in `Plan`. Accounts on the free plan can still draft
+cards, but they can't publish them nor create them through the API, and they
+are pitched an upgrade instead of the create buttons. Support can comp an
+account, or override what it counts for, from `admin/accounts`.
+
+### Stripe environment variables
+
+* `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY` — the API key
+* `STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET` — the secret `stripe listen` signs webhooks with
+* `STRIPE_UNLIMITED_PRICE_ID`, `STRIPE_UNLIMITED_PLUS_PRICE_ID` — the monthly
+  prices of the paid plans, as created in each Stripe environment
+
+Subscription changes are posted to `/stripe/webhooks`, which is where the
+account's plan comes from. Checkout and the customer portal are hosted by
+Stripe.
+
 ### Stripe environments
 
 * [Development](https://dashboard.stripe.com/acct_1SdTFtRus34tgjsJ/test/dashboard)
